okbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Peppercorn|black peppercorns]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Huckleberry|huckleberries]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n==Procedure==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 350°F.\n#In a [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|baking dish]], combine the fish stock and water. Add the salmon, making sure it is covered by liquid. If more liquid is needed, add equal parts water/fish stock until covered.\n#Add herbs, huckleberries, lemon slices, and peppercorns.\n#Place the in pan in the preheated oven, and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] for 15–18 minutes until salmon is flaky.\n#Serve and enjoy.\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Celery|Celery]], [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]], pepper, and/or [[Cookbook:Fennel|fennel]] can be added for additional flavoring.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using salmon]]\n[[Category:Poached recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using berries]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Native American recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using huckleberry]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Poached Salmon with wild Huckleberries","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"5","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 pound salmon fillet","sourceText":"1 pound salmon fillet","amountText":"1 pound salmon fillet","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup fish stock","sourceText":"1 cup fish stock","amountText":"1 cup fish stock","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup water","sourceText":"1 cup water","amountText":"1 cup water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 sprig fresh thyme","sourceText":"1 sprig fresh thyme","amountText":"1 sprig fresh thyme","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 sprig fresh parsley","sourceText":"1 sprig fresh parsley","amountText":"1 sprig fr